 "notes": "Beam EDM (Bern Ramsey cold-neutron) search for an oscillating neutron EDM from the ALP-gluon coupling. Curve digitized from the raster PNG of Fig. 4 (axionFinalAnalysis_exclusionPlot_final.png), tracing the SOLID black outline = deterministic dark-matter limit, the paper's headline result (abstract: C_G/(f_a m_a) = 2.7e13 GeV^-2 at 95% C.L. for 2e-17 to 2e-14 eV; digitized floor reproduces this within ~10%). The dotted stochastic-DM curve (factor 3.2+-0.3 weaker) is NOT reported. Figure y-axis is C_G/f_a in GeV^-1; reported as 1/f_a with C_G=1. Mass range 1e-19 to 4e-12 eV corresponds to the analyzed 23 uHz - 1 kHz band; first and last points mark the vertical edges of the exclusion region at the plot top. Local DM density assumed rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3.",
